-- Each end of the causeway, the Headland and the Lighthouse: while the
-- sea's tide is in, nobody crosses it either way. A Veto, asked of the
-- place being left before a move.

on beforeExit actor, destination, deciding
  ask world to named "sea"
  if it is not nothing and the high of the tide of it then
    put the name of the described of destination into going
    if going is "Lighthouse" then
      veto "The sea has covered the causeway. You'll have to wait for the tide to go out."
    else if going is "Headland" then
      veto "The causeway is under the sea. You're stuck here until the tide turns."
    end if
  end if
  pass beforeExit
end beforeExit
